<%# ── The headline numbers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    How many answered, and how many of them finished — as two pills over the
    map's empty half rather than as a row in the header. The map opens fitted
    to the countries that have responses, so one side of the band is reliably
    empty space; the header is where the controls belong, and the number the
    page is about does not need to compete with them for the same row.

    Rendered absolutely INSIDE the map's own stage when there is a map, and as
    an ordinary block above the feed when there is not — the band only exists
    on a Verto with region-tagged responses or two waves (see results.html.erb),
    and the count is the one thing this page must never be missing.

    `inline` picks the second form. ── %>
<div class="rmap-stats<%= " rmap-stats--inline" if local_assigns[:inline] %>">
  <% if @active_segment && @active_segment[:id] != "overall" %>
    <%# A segment's count comes from its own filtered scope, so it is NOT the
        live tally: a broadcast carrying whole-Verto totals would contradict
        the pills the filter just produced. No rate either — completion is
        only counted Verto-wide (ResultsActivity), and inventing a segment's
        would mean a second query per filter click for a number nothing else
        on the page shows. %>
    <div class="rmap-pill rmap-pill--count">
      <% if @active_segment[:suppressed] %>
        <%# A combination under the small-cell threshold: the number itself is
            the disclosure (see ResolvesResultSegments#combine_result_segments),
            so the pill says only that it is under the line. The feed says why. %>
        <span class="rh-count-num rh-count-num--under" title="<%= t("results.combination_suppressed_title") %>">&lt;<%= ResolvesResultSegments::MIN_DEMOGRAPHIC_SAMPLE %></span>
        <span class="rh-count-word">responses</span>
      <% else %>
        <span class="rh-count-num"><%= @total %></span>
        <span class="rh-count-word">response<%= @total == 1 ? "" : "s" %></span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <span class="rmap-of">of <%= @overall_total %> overall</span>
  <% else %>
    <%= turbo_stream_from(*ResultsActivity.stream_for(@survey)) %>
    <%= render "surveys/results_live",
          survey: @survey, live: false,
          **ResultsActivity.counts_for(@survey) %>
  <% end %>
</div>
